  "player_hint_1_en": "Only one square fits Carmen's clue (\"She was sitting in a chair in the Ranger Station.\"). So Carmen (C) must be at row 5, column 5. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_2_en": "Felix can't be at row 3, column 1; row 6, column 1; row 6, column 2; ...: in each case Dinah would have nowhere left to go. Suppose Felix were at row 1, column 1: then Violet would have nowhere left to go. So Felix can't be there. Testing the remaining squares the same way rules out a few more. Using the general clue (\"No one was on a bed.\"), some squares are ruled out for Felix. So Felix (F) must be at row 2, column 1. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_3_en": "Suppose Alma were at row 8, column 2: then Bianca's clue (\"She was east of Violet.\") could not be true. So Alma can't be there. So Alma (A) must be at row 7, column 2. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_4_en": "Dinah is now the only person who can still go in row 4. So Dinah (D) must be at row 4, column 4. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_5_en": "Esme is now the only person who can still go in column 3. So Esme (E) must be at row 8, column 3. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_6_en": "Gus is now the only person who can still go in row 1. So Gus (G) must be at row 1, column 7. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_7_en": "The victim must share an area with exactly one other person. So Violet (the victim) must be at row 3, column 6. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_8_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Bianca that fits her clue (\"She was east of Violet.\"). So Bianca (B) must be at row 6, column 8. Cross out her row and column. Gus is the only person in the Meadow with Violet, so Gus is the murderer!"
